===== README.md =====
executable: false

# `biome-library`

[![npm version](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/biome-library.svg)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/biome-library)
[![CI](https://github.com/hbmartin/generated-lib/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/hbmartin/generated-lib/actions/workflows/ci.yml)
[![License: ISC](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-ISC-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

A generated TypeScript library

## Install

```bash
pnpm add biome-library
```

## Usage

```ts
import { formatValue } from "biome-library";

const output = formatValue({ ready: true });
```

## CLI

```bash
biome-library --help
```

## Development

Lint, format, type-check, dependency and security policy checks, and tests are
wired into a single command:

```bash
pnpm run check         # lint + dep/security checks + typecheck + coverage
pnpm run test          # run tests
pnpm run build         # build to dist/
pnpm run release:check # package validation + publish dry run
```

`pnpm run security:lint` prefers `semgrep` on PATH and otherwise runs the pinned `uvx semgrep@1.165.0` scan.

See [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) for the conventions this project follows.

## Releasing

Publishing is automated: bump the version with `pnpm version`, push, and
publish a GitHub release. The release workflow validates the package and runs
`npm publish` with [provenance](https://docs.npmjs.com/generating-provenance-statements).

The workflow authenticates with npm
[trusted publishing](https://docs.npmjs.com/trusted-publishers) (OIDC) instead
of a long-lived token. Before the first release, add a trusted publisher on
npmjs.com for `hbmartin/generated-lib` pointing at the `release.yml` GitHub Actions
workflow.

## License

[ISC](LICENSE) © Harold Martin.

